                    <common:class level="3" classId="697dc0d1-c059-39d7-a044-f3060403e330">infrastructure</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The data on material and energy requirement for construction are taken from an old US reference using a "model diffusion plants" and are amplified by a factor of 1.2 to take into account the differences in the installed capacity of the currently operating diffusion plants (EURODIF and USEC Paducah). The land use corresponds to the USEC plant, which is presumably the most consistent with the material inventory. It is assumed that 75% of reinforced concrete is dumped as non-contaminated waste from decommissioning.;
UUID: 2d38d217-9665-31dc-adbb-229750e0e3a6</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
